  "notes": [
   "Students complete one single-language option (101 F, 102 F, 203 F, 204 F); the catalog prints 'Required Courses (18 units): 18' once over all options, recorded as stated 18 on each option block.",
   "Restricted Electives or Substitution Courses are used only by students placed above 101 F (or native Spanish speakers following SPAN 201 F-SPAN 204 F) to reach the 18-22 unit total; no unit minimum is printed for the block, so minimum is null.",
   "The restricted electives list also allows 'A second foreign language (any course from 101 F through 204 F)', with no specific codes printed.",
   "ENGL C1002 is printed without units.",
   "The catalog prints ANTH 105 F and ANTH 105HF as 'or' options under SPAN 205 F; recorded as alternatives as printed, which may be a formatting artifact.",
   "Closed list stores 'JAPN 101 f' (lowercase); the catalog prints 'JAPN 101 F', treated as the same course.",
   "Footnote: students may not receive credit for SPAN 101 F or SPAN 102 F and SPAN 201 F; native speakers take SPAN 201 F then SPAN 204 F and complete remaining units from restricted electives.",
